From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pvr: Advertise linear filtering for linear (strided) 2D images

Linear images are always 2D, single layer and single level, and the TPU
filters strided textures in 2D (the driver already sets the IMG-specific
FILTER_LINEAR_2D bit). Without the core bit, dma-buf textures (only
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR is supported) can't be filtered: the wlroots Vulkan
renderer found no usable texture format and aborted (dmabuf feedback
table empty).

Tested: cage starts with WLR_RENDERER=vulkan; RetroArch (now using its
linear streamed-texture path) shows the game correctly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JJfik1hpStPgtN7deJRwXG
---
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_formats.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_formats.c
@@ -290,7 +290,15 @@
          if (!vk_format_is_int(vk_format) &&
              !vk_format_is_depth_or_stencil(vk_format) &&
              first_component_size < 32) {
-            flags |= VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR_2D_BIT_IMG;
+            /* Linear images are always 2D, single layer and single level
+             * here (see pvr_get_image_format_properties), and the TPU filters
+             * strided textures in 2D, so the core bit is valid too. Without
+             * it, dma-buf textures (only DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR is supported)
+             * can't be filtered: the wlroots Vulkan renderer finds no usable
+             * format at all, and GL-on-Vulkan copies them first.
+             */
+            flags |= VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR_2D_BIT_IMG |
+                     VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR_BIT;
          }
 
          if (ycbcr_info) {
